00:04:05,806 --> 00:04:11,806
A hero will be revealed.

2
00:08:11,612 --> 00:08:17,612
Spider-Man 2 is a action, adventure, science fiction film directed by Sam Raimi.

3
00:12:17,419 --> 00:12:23,419
Peter Parker is going through a major identity crisis.

4
00:16:23,225 --> 00:16:29,225
Burned out from being Spider-Man, he decides to shelve his superhero alter ego, which
leaves the city suffering in the wake of carnage left by the evil Doc Ock.

5
00:20:29,032 --> 00:20:35,032
In the meantime, Parker still can't act on his feelings for Mary
Jane Watson, a girl he's loved since childhood.

6
00:24:34,838 --> 00:24:40,838
A certain anger begins to brew in his best friend Harry Osborn as well...

7
00:28:40,645 --> 00:28:46,645
Spider-Man / Peter Parker, played by Tobey Maguire.

8
00:32:46,451 --> 00:32:52,451
Mary Jane Watson, played by Kirsten Dunst.

9
00:36:52,258 --> 00:36:58,258
Harry Osborn, played by James Franco.

10
00:40:58,064 --> 00:41:04,064
Doc Ock / Otto Octavius, played by Alfred Molina.

11
00:45:03,870 --> 00:45:09,870
May Parker, played by Rosemary Harris.

12
00:49:09,677 --> 00:49:15,677
J. Jonah Jameson, played by J.K. Simmons.

13
00:53:15,483 --> 00:53:21,483
Spider-Man 2 is a 2004 American superhero film based on
the Marvel Comics character Spider-Man.

14
00:57:21,290 --> 00:57:27,290
Directed by Sam Raimi and written by Alvin Sargent from a story conceived by Michael Chabon and the writing team of Alfred
Gough and Miles Millar, it is the second installment in Raimi's Spider-Man trilogy, following the 2002 film.

15
01:01:27,096 --> 01:01:33,096
The film stars Tobey Maguire as Peter Parker / Spider-Man, alongside Kirsten
Dunst, James Franco, Alfred Molina, Rosemary Harris, and Donna Murphy.

16
01:05:32,903 --> 01:05:38,903
Peter Parker fights to stop scientist Dr.

17
01:09:38,709 --> 01:09:44,709
Otto Octavius from recreating a dangerous experiment,
while also dealing with a personal crisis.

18
01:13:44,516 --> 01:13:50,516
Principal photography began in April 2003 in New York
City and also took place in Los Angeles.

19
01:17:50,322 --> 01:17:56,322
Reshoots took place later that year and concluded in February 2004.

20
01:21:56,129 --> 01:22:02,129
Danny Elfman returned to compose the score.

21
01:26:01,935 --> 01:26:07,935
Spider-Man 2 premiered at the Mann Village Theater in Los Angeles on June 25, 2004,
and was released in both conventional and IMAX theaters on June 30.

22
01:30:07,741 --> 01:30:13,741
It received acclaim from critics, who praised its emotional weight and visual
effects, the performances of Maguire and Molina, and Raimi's directing.

23
01:34:13,548 --> 01:34:19,548
The film grossed $795.9 million worldwide, making it the
third-highest-grossing film of the year.

24
01:38:19,354 --> 01:38:25,354
It was selected by the American Film Institute as
one of the top 10 films of 2004.

25
01:42:25,161 --> 01:42:31,161
Spider-Man 2 won Best Visual Effects at the 77th Academy Awards, and was
also nominated for Best Sound Mixing and Best Sound Editing.

26
01:46:30,967 --> 01:46:36,967
It received five awards at the Saturn Awards, including
Best Fantasy Film and Best Director.

27
01:50:36,774 --> 01:50:42,774
Its success led to Spider-Man 3 (2007).

28
01:54:42,580 --> 01:54:48,580
The Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU) film Spider-Man: No Way Home (2021) explored the concept of the multiverse to
connect the previous Spider-Man films to the MCU, with Maguire and Molina reprising their roles.

29
01:58:48,387 --> 01:58:54,387
The film explores themes of new york city, dual identity,
love of one's life, secret identity, superhero.

30
02:02:54,193 --> 02:03:00,193
The tone is thought_provoking.
